\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {16}{\ignorespaces Diamond configuration atom diagrams. (Left) Duplicate of Fig.\nobreakspace  {}\ref {FirstDiamondAtom} placed for convenience. A diamond configuration atomic system with non-degenerate energy levels $\ket  {1}, \ket  {2}, \ket  {3}, \ket  {4}$. The system has allowed transitions $\ket  {1} \leftrightarrow \ket  {2}$, $\ket  {1} \leftrightarrow \ket  {3}$, $\ket  {2} \leftrightarrow \ket  {4}$, and $\ket  {3} \leftrightarrow \ket  {4}$ with respective energies $\hbar \omega _{12}$, $\hbar \omega _{13}$, $\hbar \omega _{24}$, and $\hbar \omega _{34}$ and corresponding wavelengths $\lambda _{12}$, $\lambda _{13}$, $\lambda _{24}$, and $\lambda _{34}$. (Right) A strong pump drives transition $\ket  {1} \leftrightarrow \ket  {3}$ at frequency $\omega _I$ with detuning $\Delta _I = \omega _I - \omega _{13}$, a separate strong pump drives transition $\ket  {2} \leftrightarrow \ket  {4}$ with detuning $\Delta _{II} = \omega _{II} - \omega _{24}$, a weak signal beam drives transition $\ket  {1} \leftrightarrow \ket  {2}$ with detuning $\Delta _{s} = \omega _{s} - \omega _{12}$, and a weak idler field (undriven) is induced by the presence of the other fields through a FWM process, resulting in transition $\ket  {3} \leftrightarrow \ket  {4}$ with emission detuning $\Delta _{i} = \omega _{i} - \omega _{34}$.\relax }}{31}{figure.caption.19}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:twosidebyside}{{16}{31}{Diamond configuration atom diagrams. (Left) Duplicate of Fig.~\ref {FirstDiamondAtom} placed for convenience. A diamond configuration atomic system with non-degenerate energy levels $\ket {1}, \ket {2}, \ket {3}, \ket {4}$. The system has allowed transitions $\ket {1} \leftrightarrow \ket {2}$, $\ket {1} \leftrightarrow \ket {3}$, $\ket {2} \leftrightarrow \ket {4}$, and $\ket {3} \leftrightarrow \ket {4}$ with respective energies $\hbar \omega _{12}$, $\hbar \omega _{13}$, $\hbar \omega _{24}$, and $\hbar \omega _{34}$ and corresponding wavelengths $\lambda _{12}$, $\lambda _{13}$, $\lambda _{24}$, and $\lambda _{34}$. (Right) A strong pump drives transition $\ket {1} \leftrightarrow \ket {3}$ at frequency $\omega _I$ with detuning $\Delta _I = \omega _I - \omega _{13}$, a separate strong pump drives transition $\ket {2} \leftrightarrow \ket {4}$ with detuning $\Delta _{II} = \omega _{II} - \omega _{24}$, a weak signal beam drives transition $\ket {1} \leftrightarrow \ket {2}$ with detuning $\Delta _{s} = \omega _{s} - \omega _{12}$, and a weak idler field (undriven) is induced by the presence of the other fields through a FWM process, resulting in transition $\ket {3} \leftrightarrow \ket {4}$ with emission detuning $\Delta _{i} = \omega _{i} - \omega _{34}$.\relax }{figure.caption.19}{}}
